==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Earlier spelling was ''inhiminen'', compare [[inhimillinen]].

{{unk|fi}} origin, perhaps from Proto-Indo-European *ǵnh₁- ''"[[kin]]"'', (see [[w:Laryngeal_theory#Evidence_from_Uralic|laryngeal theory]]). Cognate with Estonian {{m|et|inimene}} and Karelian {{m|krl|ihmini}}, old Finnish {{m|fi|inehmo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈiçmine̞n]|lang=fi}}
* {{audio|fi-ihminen.ogg|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|ih|mi|nen|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|inen|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# A [[human being]].
# A [[person]].
# As a former part of compound (as the stem '''''ihmis-''''') signifying [[human]].

